---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title='Prowlarr Search Privacy Policy'>
  <main class='privacy-shell'>
    <section class='privacy-card'>
      <header class='privacy-header'>
        <p class='eyebrow'>Chrome Extension</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy for Prowlarr Search</h1>
        <p class='updated'>Last Updated: April 1, 2026</p>
      </header>

      <p>
        Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how the
        <strong> Prowlarr Search </strong>
        Chrome extension handles your data.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information Collection and Use</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Prowlarr Search</strong> is designed to be a private and secure
        tool for searching your own Prowlarr instance.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Prowlarr Server Data:</strong> The extension requires you to
          provide the URL and API key of your own Prowlarr server. This
          information is used solely to communicate with your server to perform
          searches and retrieve results.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Search Queries:</strong> When you use the extension to search,
          the search terms are sent directly to
          <strong> your configured Prowlarr server</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Centralized Tracking:</strong> We do not collect, store, or
          monitor your search queries, the results you receive, or any other
          usage data. There is no central server that tracks your activity.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Data Storage</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local Storage:</strong> Your Prowlarr URL, API key, and search
          preferences (categories, selected indexers) are stored using the
          <code>chrome.storage.sync</code> API.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Chrome Sync:</strong> If you have Chrome Sync enabled, this
          data may be synced across your devices by Google to provide a
          consistent experience. This data is encrypted by Google during transit
          and at rest according to their privacy standards.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Third-Party Access:</strong> We do not have access to the
          data stored in your browser or your Prowlarr server.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Data Disclosure</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Direct Communication:</strong> The extension only sends data to
          the URL you explicitly provide in the settings. No data is sent to any
          other third party, including the developer of this extension.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Sale of Data:</strong> We do not sell, trade, or otherwise
          transfer your information to outside parties.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Permissions</h2>
      <p>The extension requests the following permissions to function:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>storage</code>: To save your Prowlarr configuration.</li>
        <li>
          <code>contextMenus</code>: To allow you to right-click selected text
          and search Prowlarr.
        </li>
        <li><code>activeTab</code>: To facilitate the display of search results.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Host Permissions:</strong> To allow the extension to make API
          requests to the Prowlarr server URL you provide.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be
        reflected in the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact the
        developer through the Chrome Web Store support page or the project's
        repository.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-shell {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw + 1rem, 3.5rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 500px at -5% -15%, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.14), transparent 50%),
      radial-gradient(900px 450px at 110% 0%, rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.1), transparent 45%);
  }

  .privacy-card {
    width: min(920px, 100%);
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 2.1vw + 1rem, 3rem);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      150deg,
      rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.94),
      rgba(18, 18, 18, 0.92)
    );
    box-shadow:
      0 14px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45),
      inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  }

  .privacy-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: #67e8f9;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0.45rem 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.3vw + 1rem, 2.45rem);
    line-height: 1.18;
    color: #f9fafb;
  }

  .updated {
    margin: 0;
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 0.6vw + 0.95rem, 1.35rem);
    color: #e2e8f0;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: #d1d5db;
    line-height: 1.72;
    font-size: clamp(0.98rem, 0.2vw + 0.93rem, 1.06rem);
  }

  ul {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: 0.42rem;
  }

  strong {
    color: #f1f5f9;
  }

  code {
    background: rgba(2, 132, 199, 0.18);
    border: 1px solid rgba(125, 211, 252, 0.26);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.36rem;
    color: #e0f2fe;
    font-size: 0.93em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .privacy-card {
      border-radius: 14px;
    }

    ul {
      padding-left: 1.05rem;
    }
  }
</style>
